1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:01,477
This is PACT.

2
00:00:01,477 --> 00:00:05,955
It's a drone delivery fleet that keeps working, even when the central brain goes dark.

3
00:00:11,100 --> 00:00:15,670
Right now, most delivery fleets lean on one central controller and a solid radio link.

4
00:00:15,670 --> 00:00:17,795
If you lose that hub, every drone stops.

5
00:00:17,795 --> 00:00:22,153
And if the radio splits, two groups of drones can end up claiming the same parcel.

6
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:30,788
PACT gets rid of the central controller.

7
00:00:30,788 --> 00:00:36,758
Every drone runs the same logic, and it only talks to the drones it can actually reach by radio.

8
00:00:36,758 --> 00:00:40,986
They bid for jobs based on priority, distance, deadline and battery.

9
00:00:40,986 --> 00:00:46,272
Each drone keeps its own copy of the order board, and those copies sync up by gossip.

10
00:00:52,900 --> 00:00:57,671
So here's the same city, the same seed and the same orders, run twice.

11
00:00:57,671 --> 00:01:00,874
On the left, a central hub hands out every job.

12
00:01:00,874 --> 00:01:03,191
Three minutes in, we kill the hub.

13
00:01:03,191 --> 00:01:06,189
The central fleet stops picking up new work.

14
00:01:06,189 --> 00:01:10,755
PACT doesn't have anything central to lose, so it just keeps going:

15
00:01:10,755 --> 00:01:14,913
eighty-six percent on time, the same as with no fault at all.

16
00:01:22,367 --> 00:01:26,706
Now let's split the fleet in two over the radio, for five minutes.

17
00:01:26,706 --> 00:01:34,792
Both halves keep working, and every claim carries an epoch and a lease, so a depot only hands a parcel to its newest owner.

18
00:01:34,792 --> 00:01:40,446
Across two hundred and forty runs with radio splits, PACT made zero double deliveries.

19
00:01:40,446 --> 00:01:43,404
A plain auction made nearly eighteen per run.

20
00:01:52,367 --> 00:01:55,284
If a drone fails mid-delivery, it just goes quiet.

21
00:01:55,284 --> 00:02:03,977
The drones that were expecting to hear from it report the silence, its depot marks it as failed, and exactly one replacement job goes out to auction.

22
00:02:13,733 --> 00:02:15,989
And it's not just a browser demo.

23
00:02:15,989 --> 00:02:19,339
The same protocol runs as real robotics software:

24
00:02:19,339 --> 00:02:29,662
ROS 2 lifecycle components, one container per drone, quadrotor physics in Gazebo, and PX4 autopilots in the loop, all over an authenticated mesh radio.

25
00:02:39,300 --> 00:02:41,080
Every run is deterministic.

26
00:02:41,080 --> 00:02:47,079
The same seed gives you the same event log, and the replay viewer checks it event by event.

27
00:02:47,079 --> 00:02:54,857
Nearly a thousand automated tests pass across both simulators, and there's a public benchmark against three baselines.

28
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:04,723
Today, PACT is a simulation prototype, and real hardware is the next step.

29
00:03:04,723 --> 00:03:07,330
No hub, no double deliveries, no stalls.

